From f2164c2d4c481cda58986bc6f7f0a3880b9cb386 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Russell Ballestrini <russell@unturf.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] b43: AC-PHY: turn the verified BCM4360 feature set on by default

The bring-up parameters stay available for comparison; their defaults
become the set verified on the Netgear R6400 against a 2x2 client
(2026-10-08): radio power-on, wl's PHY reset pulse, HT40 with the 40 MHz
power rows, A-MPDU RX/TX with the status fixes, multi-rate retries, AP
power save, the HT-dead restart safety net, hardware CCMP, the per-frame
fast path, 2 spatial streams and the aggregate length limits (124 / 132
Mbit/s over the air, MCS 15 both ways).
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c   |  4 ++--
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_ac.c | 20 +++++++-------
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c   | 36 ++++++++++++------------
 3 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

